ustomers happy with our results is our main objective"}], "selected": 0, "correct": false, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ", that's why "}], "selected": 0, "correct": false, "id": 1}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "the Pareto Principle gets issues analyzed."}], "selected": 0, "correct": true, "id": 2, "text": ""}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": " Besides that,"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 3, "text": ""}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "it also has information explained and it has the defect tracking process interpreted. "}], "selected": 0, "correct": true, "id": 4, "text": ""}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "80% of the mistakes are in the 20% of the code; "}], "selected": 0, "correct": false, "id": 5, "text": ""}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "the principle has these defects illustrated,"}], "selected": 0, "correct": true, "id": 6, "text": ""}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": " so any programmer can notice them.  "}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 7, "text": ""}], "id": 0}], "type": "SLS", "template_override": 1, "id": 9}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "RSLT", "template_override": 1, "id": 10}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Let's research about Pareto Principle."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob05re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1, "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n8le01ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Sophia</span>: So, the software development team was lagging behind because they were tracking defects?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Charlee:</span>: Not exactly. Every organization should have their defects tracked in order to get them fixed and to help find patterns of where most defects are coming from. However, our greatest trouble was having unnecessary data entered by the members of the team; thus, they were losing too much time when tracking defects to the point where this process became ineffective. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Sophia</span>: But I thought having detailed information entered could enrich the database and facilitate the fixing process."}, {"time": "38800", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "For this reason, in order to know when tracking defects is truly necessary, I suggest having some questions addressed to get to know more about how this process should be carried out. These question are: What are the most common types of defects that are causing most of the problems in software quality? When are these defects injected into the product? Who is going to use the collected data for tracked defects? And how is this data going to help improve the product? <br>"}, {"time": "74800", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "These questions respond to the Pareto Principle in which most likely, most defects are found in one or two processes. As we need to be effective and aim to improve quality, we must have the defects that affect the software development process the most tracked with more attention and detail. If every organization has their most relevant defects prioritized, they can improve their defect tracking process just as the Pareto Principle suggests.<br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n8le01ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 4, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}